  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Every quadratic can be solved — and when the discriminant is negative, the solutions live in the <strong>complex numbers</strong>. This chapter ties graphing, factoring and the imaginary unit together.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 2.1 — The imaginary unit",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Define \\( i=\\sqrt{-1} \\), so \\( i^{2}=-1 \\). A <strong>complex number</strong> has the form \\( a+bi \\) with \\( a,b \\) real; add and multiply just as with binomials, replacing \\( i^{2} \\) by \\( -1 \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Quadratic formula",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x=\\dfrac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Discriminant",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\Delta=b^{2}-4ac \\) decides the root type",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Vertex",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x=-\\dfrac{b}{2a} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Powers of i",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( i^{2}=-1,\\ i^{3}=-i,\\ i^{4}=1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Describe the roots of \\( x^{2}+2x+5=0 \\).</p><p>Discriminant \\( \\Delta=2^{2}-4(1)(5)=-16&lt;0 \\), so there are no real roots — two complex conjugates. Solving:</p>\\[ x=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{-16}}{2}=-1\\pm 2i. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Multiply \\( (2+i)(3-i) \\).</p>\\[ 6-2i+3i-i^{2}=6+i+1=7+i. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve \\(x^2-4x+13=0\\) and express roots in the form \\(a\\pm bi\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Discriminant \\(=16-52=-36\\). \\(x=\\dfrac{4\\pm\\sqrt{-36}}{2}=\\dfrac{4\\pm6i}{2}=2\\pm3i\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
